{
  "description": "an on_click handler body runs in the environment captured at REGISTRATION, not the one current when the click is delivered. The handler is registered inside setup and fires from the top-level wait, after setup has returned, so :v exists only in the registration environment - printing 7 is possible only if that environment was captured and used, and resolving against the delivery-time scope raises ol-undefined-var instead. Completes the set with every-body-runs-in-registration-environment and on-key-body-runs-in-registration-environment (issue #828), so all four handler kinds now assert the property stack-neutrally rather than only the one where a regression happened to be caught. Pins capture of the ENVIRONMENT, not of values: nothing is snapshotted",
